---

# The same rule inside a body

Nothing about a parameterless method depends on where it is declared, and the top-level case is
covered by `parameterless-def-mention`. This case exists because the two are separate code paths in
every lane, and measuring them separately is what showed the top-level one green while the local one
was not.

The v2 half is the worse failure: it exits **0** and prints `<closure>` for every line, so a program
that mis-invokes here produces a plausible wrong answer instead of an error.

js was red here too. Its emitter had the right rule and an incomplete input: `zeroParamFns`, which
decides whether a bare name is emitted as `mk` or `mk()`, was filled by the TOP-LEVEL pre-pass only,
so the identical declaration one scope deeper emitted `_dispatch(mk, 'v', [])` — the function object
instead of its value.

```scalascript
case class Box(v: String)
def main(): Unit =
  def mk: Box = Box("loc")
  var n = 0
  def next: Int =
    n = n + 1
    n
  println(mk.v)
  println(next)
  println(next)
```
